 INPUT CARD>! Why this file exists                                                          
 INPUT CARD>! ============================================================                  
 INPUT CARD>! caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPPb/c/d all showed the same pathology: energy          
 INPUT CARD>! dropping far faster than the geometry was moving, and a growing negative      
 INPUT CARD>! Hessian curvature from the very first optimization step. TZVPPd (IHREP=2,     
 INPUT CARD>! forcing a genuinely fresh Hessian every 2 steps rather than one slowly        
 INPUT CARD>! propagated by BFGS) gave the decisive evidence: at NSERCH=2 and NSERCH=3,     
 INPUT CARD>! TWO INDEPENDENTLY COMPUTED Hessians each showed 15 SIMULTANEOUS NEGATIVE      
 INPUT CARD>! EIGENVALUES, closely matching each other in value. That rules out numerical   
 INPUT CARD>! noise (noise does not reproduce like that) and confirms this is a real        
 INPUT CARD>! feature of the wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP/PCM(water) surface at this geometry: it     
 INPUT CARD>! is not a stationary point of any kind, let alone a minimum.                   
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! The source of the mismatch was then found directly: caa005bIRC.cml (the       
 INPUT CARD>! 290-point IRC this starting geometry was extracted from, at Reaction          
 INPUT CARD>! Coordinate step 1) was NOT computed at wB97X-D/def2-TZVPP. Its embedded       
 INPUT CARD>! basis set exponents (e.g. carbon 1S: 3047.52, 456.424, 103.653, 29.2258,      
 INPUT CARD>! 9.34863, 3.18904) match the classic Pople 6-31G(d) contraction, not           
 INPUT CARD>! def2-TZVPP -- and its reported energies (~-765.89) differ from ours           
 INPUT CARD>! (~-491.67) by ~274 Hartree, far too large to be a basis-quality effect        
 INPUT CARD>! alone, strongly suggesting a different method entirely generated this path.   
 INPUT CARD>! A geometry that is a good minimum on one PES has no reason to be anywhere     
 INPUT CARD>! near a stationary point on a different one -- 15 negative eigenvalues is      
 INPUT CARD>! entirely consistent with that, not evidence of a technical mistake.           
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
